{
  "//": "§8.2 Telegram attestation. init_data = raw Telegram.WebApp.initData minus one hash=<v> pair (the first) and one adjacent '&' (raw_init_data_with_hash shows the original; its hash uses a fake bot token and is never checked); a second hash pair is left in place and refused (second_hash_pair_kept_by_removal). Verifier, in order (why): (1) split on '&', key/value at the first '='; decode %XX and '+'->space; per pair, in order: no '=' (parse_no_equals), bad % (parse_percent), non-UTF-8 result (parse_utf8), empty key (parse_empty_key), a raw LF in the decoded key or value (lf), a raw CR there (cr), '=' in the decoded key (key_eq), duplicate key (parse_duplicate) -> attest_bad, all before the signature (lf/key_eq would let the data-check string be re-split under the same signature: resplit_data_check_string / signed_data_check_string verify with the test key; a CR re-splits nothing but is refused by the same rule: cr_in_value, cr_in_key, signed as they are); hash present -> attest_has_hash. (2) auth_date, user, signature, start_param required (missing_<name>). (3) data-check-string = \"<bot_id>:WebAppData\\n\" + all pairs except signature sorted bytewise by key as key=<decoded value>, joined by \\n. (4) signature: exactly 86 characters without '=' or 88 ending in '==' (a single '=' is invalid), else strict base64url, 64 bytes (signature_format); all-zero key always refused (zero_key); Ed25519 with keys.json telegram_test_ed25519 or verify_key_hex (signature). (5) start_param == \"k_\" + new_key_id (start_param). (6) user is a JSON object with integer id in 1..2^53-1 (user_id). Values are encoded like Telegram (encodeURIComponent, user JSON with \\/), so '+' in photo_url travels as %2B. Decoding goes by Unicode code points (a raw astral character is one character, its UTF-8 4 bytes: raw_astral_character_in_user) and keeps a leading U+FEFF in a value (value_with_leading_bom_kept: the signature covers the BOM; a BOM-stripping decoder rebuilds bom_stripped_data_check_string and fails). init_data over 4096 bytes is refused earlier as proof_invalid:malformed (recover.json). Consumers assert both the verdict (expect) and `why` of every negative case: several cases are built so that a verifier missing one rule reaches a different verdict, and `why` names the rule that must refuse first.",
